      "updated": 1781398945274,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is LangChain?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is LangChain?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kjtr3GvbZn-dOwitRB6iJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1246.9482002877426,
      "y": 99468.36512909946,
      "width": 1155,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "btd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1314841100,
      "version": 739,
      "versionNonce": 928147122,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781398945274,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Langchain is a open source library designed to simplify the process of building LLM based\napplications.\nIt provides modular building blocks, that let us create LLM based workflows with ease.\n\nLangchaing consists of multiple components\n1. Model components gives us a unified interface to interact with various LLM providers.\n2. Prompts component helps us engineer prompts\n3. Retriever components helps us fetch relevant documents from a vector store.\n\nBut the biggest offering of LangChain in chains. we can create chain by adding different diff components.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Langchain is a open source library designed to simplify the process of building LLM based\napplications.\nIt provides modular building blocks, that let us create LLM based workflows with ease.\n\nLangchaing consists of multiple components\n1. Model components gives us a unified interface to interact with various LLM providers.\n2. Prompts component helps us engineer prompts\n3. Retriever components helps us fetch relevant documents from a vector store.\n\nBut the biggest offering of LangChain in chains. we can create chain by adding different diff components.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
