    {
      "id": "FpYQs3XO9fzbKejNZeN-q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1297.3446846627426,
      "y": 107928.32411347446,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bwL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2006637482,
      "version": 1207,
      "versionNonce": 2097230894,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781398945275,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "this is not a challenge more of feature, we have talked about workflow, if we want to create\nworkflow inside workflow then we can do that. We can represent any workflow as a graph in Lang\nGraph where each node representing one task. SInce we can create subgraph hence we can create\nany type of nested workflow as well.\n\nConduct interview itself is a big task\n1 we are preparing qus for each candidate\n2 Multiple rounds of interview with evaluation\nsince all the things are done in one conduct interview only, so we can treat this as one nested\nworkflow, and we can connect this nested workflow in our bigger workflow. So we can create\nany no of workflows inside one workflow. And we represent a workflow as a node in our graph.\n\nSo we can create multi agent system with  this nested workflow or using subgraph in LangGraph.\nWith Subgraph we can make our code reusable.  we can create one subgraph for some feature that\nwe can use in multiple place in bigger task.\n\nFor LangChain it is a challenge.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "this is not a challenge more of feature, we have talked about workflow, if we want to create\nworkflow inside workflow then we can do that. We can represent any workflow as a graph in Lang\nGraph where each node representing one task. SInce we can create subgraph hence we can create\nany type of nested workflow as well.\n\nConduct interview itself is a big task\n1 we are preparing qus for each candidate\n2 Multiple rounds of interview with evaluation\nsince all the things are done in one conduct interview only, so we can treat this as one nested\nworkflow, and we can connect this nested workflow in our bigger workflow. So we can create\nany no of workflows inside one workflow. And we represent a workflow as a node in our graph.\n\nSo we can create multi agent system with  this nested workflow or using subgraph in LangGraph.\nWith Subgraph we can make our code reusable.  we can create one subgraph for some feature that\nwe can use in multiple place in bigger task.\n\nFor LangChain it is a challenge.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZtorK2gZksa6RAqZsq3-c",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1215.3798409127426,
      "y": 108443.83973847446,
      "width": 308,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
