      "updated": 1781398945275,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Challenge 7 -> Observability",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Challenge 7 -> Observability",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9MNCWmRv5TGj60SwxAW7q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1275.3017159127426,
      "y": 108477.30848847446,
      "width": 1111,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bwN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2087914602,
      "version": 1669,
      "versionNonce": 593919598,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781398945275,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "observability refers to how easily we can monitor, debug and understand what your workflow is doing\nat runtime\n\nwe have one library named LangSmith using whihc we can monitor our LLM application in LangChain.\nit will record everything when we have called LLM, what was the prompt, what was the reply, what\nwas the time take, howmany tokens everything LangSmith will record. LangSmith can only monitor\nLangchain but can't monitor our Glue code. It means if we are createing Complex workflow using\nLangchain & Langsmith, we will get only partial observabitlity as it can't observer glue code.\n\n\nWith LangGraph, LangSmith has too tight intergration, in LangGraph whole timeline of events like\nfrom this node to this node everything record in LangSmith. everything Human intervention when\nhuman approval came, when we have aksed for the input, and what is the node before that everything\nLangSmith records. Hence we can backtrack whole workflow using LangSmith.\n\nwhen we deploy our workflow in production, we must monitor very closly. with LangChain we can only\nmonitor partially due to gluecode, but if we are using LangGraph to build our complex workflow, since\nwe are writing everything in LangGraph ,hence LangGraph can tell very well to LangSmith what was\nthe reason for taking this decision at each and every point. it makes monitoring, observability\nvery easy.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "observability refers to how easily we can monitor, debug and understand what your workflow is doing\nat runtime\n\nwe have one library named LangSmith using whihc we can monitor our LLM application in LangChain.\nit will record everything when we have called LLM, what was the prompt, what was the reply, what\nwas the time take, howmany tokens everything LangSmith will record. LangSmith can only monitor\nLangchain but can't monitor our Glue code. It means if we are createing Complex workflow using\nLangchain & Langsmith, we will get only partial observabitlity as it can't observer glue code.\n\n\nWith LangGraph, LangSmith has too tight intergration, in LangGraph whole timeline of events like\nfrom this node to this node everything record in LangSmith. everything Human intervention when\nhuman approval came, when we have aksed for the input, and what is the node before that everything\nLangSmith records. Hence we can backtrack whole workflow using LangSmith.\n\nwhen we deploy our workflow in production, we must monitor very closly. with LangChain we can only\nmonitor partially due to gluecode, but if we are using LangGraph to build our complex workflow, since\nwe are writing everything in LangGraph ,hence LangGraph can tell very well to LangSmith what was\nthe reason for taking this decision at each and every point. it makes monitoring, observability\nvery easy.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JUkp9pKf0N_Es2kFncrhe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1154.3798409127426,
      "y": 109048.83973847446,
      "width": 143,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
