      "text": "Reducers ->",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Reducers ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EIordcH2rtxmHglLm6TqS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1426.3832403912888,
      "y": 113697.31463207127,
      "width": 1012,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bzq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 703192878,
      "version": 288,
      "versionNonce": 1036304242,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781404814458,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reducers in LangGraph define how updates from nodes are applied to the shared state.\nEach key in the state can have its own reducer, which determines whether new data replaces, \nmerges or adds to the existing value.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Reducers in LangGraph define how updates from nodes are applied to the shared state.\nEach key in the state can have its own reducer, which determines whether new data replaces, \nmerges or adds to the existing value.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6Np53oDTDcllhq5Wcu_IE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1369.4455156419936,
      "y": 113877.41085606732,
      "width": 308,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bzr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2116053618,
      "version": 35,
      "versionNonce": 123448818,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781404130121,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "LangGraph Execution Model ->",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "LangGraph Execution Model ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "msx5o1veJeBXX5j_gRGDk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1409.7605949976507,
      "y": 113913.52284704929,
      "width": 1056,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bzs",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 611952878,
      "version": 1157,
      "versionNonce": 2146622642,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781404817095,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Graph Definition ->\n    we define\n    - The state schema\n    - Nodes(Functions that performs tasks)\n    - Edges(Which node connects to which)\n\n\n2 Compilation ->\n    we call .compile() on the StateGraph\n    this checks the graph structure and prepare it for execution\n\n3 Invocation ->\n    We run the graph with .invoke(initial_state)\n    LangGraph sends the initial state as a message to the entry node(s).\n\n4 Super Step Begin ->\n    Whole workflow devided into super steps, one super step can have one step or multiple steps.\n    Execution proceeds in round\n    in each round(superstep)\n    - All active nodes(those that received messages) run in parallel\n    - Each returns an update(message) to state.\n\n5 Message passing & Node Activation\n    The message are passed to down stream nodes via edges.\n    Nodes that receive messages become active for the next round.\n\n6 Halting Condition ->\n    No nodes are active, and\n    no messages are in transit(no message pass in edges)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Graph Definition ->\n    we define\n    - The state schema\n    - Nodes(Functions that performs tasks)\n    - Edges(Which node connects to which)\n\n\n2 Compilation ->\n    we call .compile() on the StateGraph\n    this checks the graph structure and prepare it for execution\n\n3 Invocation ->\n    We run the graph with .invoke(initial_state)\n    LangGraph sends the initial state as a message to the entry node(s).\n\n4 Super Step Begin ->\n    Whole workflow devided into super steps, one super step can have one step or multiple steps.\n    Execution proceeds in round\n    in each round(superstep)\n    - All active nodes(those that received messages) run in parallel\n    - Each returns an update(message) to state.\n\n5 Message passing & Node Activation\n    The message are passed to down stream nodes via edges.\n    Nodes that receive messages become active for the next round.\n\n6 Halting Condition ->\n    No nodes are active, and\n    no messages are in transit(no message pass in edges)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
